; Print string number A at the text cursor, aligned
;
; Finds string A in the text table (#R$9F43), measures it (#R$9F52), lets #R$9F75 set the cursor x from the alignment
; mode (#R$9F93) and the width, then draws the characters one at a time with #R$9E79, each advancing the cursor by its
; width. The cursor y is not changed; HL ends after the string. Reached from script codes $85 (string number in the
; script, #R$9DAF) and $84 (string number read from a variable, #R$9DB7).
; .
; Hardware: draws the proportional font into the screen bitmap by XOR (through #R$9E79); the attributes are not
; touched, so the text takes the colours the cells already have.
;
; A String number 0-52 (the text table at $9048)
@label=PrintString
c$9F30 CALL $9F43    ;
 $9F33 CALL $9F52    ;
 $9F36 CALL $9F75    ;
 $9F39 LD B,(HL)     ; string length
 $9F3A INC HL        ;
@label=PrintString_Loop
*$9F3B LD A,(HL)     ;
 $9F3C INC HL        ;
 $9F3D CALL $9E79    ;
 $9F40 DJNZ $9F3B    ;
 $9F42 RET           ;
